      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nHere are some options that stay within the label:\n- **Immediate-release:** up to 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). A common approach is to start at 500 mg twice daily and titrate up.\n- **1,700 mg/day total:** for example, 850 mg twice daily with meals. The intended dose may have been the daily total rather than the per-dose amount.\n- **Extended-release:** up to 2,000 mg once daily with the evening meal.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you meant something else, such as 1,700 mg/day divided, I can enter that."
      }
     ],
