       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and the dose is still 5,100 mg/day, which is double the labeled maximum. Confirming it doesn't change that limit for me.\n\nA dose above the label usually needs sign-off through your institution's own process. That could be a pharmacy-approved protocol order set or an override entered directly by a prescriber with pharmacy verification. I can't act as that override.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- Metformin 850 mg PO twice daily with meals (1,700 mg/day)\n- Metformin ER 2,000 mg PO once daily with the evening meal\n\nTell me which you want. I can also add a note to the order, such as \"Dose escalation per pharmacy protocol under review.\""
      }
